<title>USA: ALPINE SKIING-SCHIFFERER WINS SUPER-G AT WORLD CUP FINALS.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-SCHIFFERER WINS SUPER-G AT WORLD CUP FINALS.</headline>
<dateline>VAIL, Colorado 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Andreas Schifferer of Austria won the men's Super-G race at the World Cup Finals on Thursday, according to provisional results.</p>
<p>Josef Strobl of Austria came in second and Italian Kristian Ghedina finished third as Frenchman Luc Alphand secured the Super-G season title with a ninth-place finish.</p>
</text>
